{# The cloud itself.

   Each word carries the size App\Service\WordCloud\WordCloudWeighting gave it and the rung of the
   colour ladder it sits on. The rule lives in PHP alone, so the pilot preview, the board and the
   live refresh can never draw the same cloud differently; the *colour* of a rung is a class, left
   to the stylesheet, because the pilot preview sits on a white card in the light theme and on a
   dark one in the other.

   The words arrive already laid out centre-outwards, so a centred flex-wrap puts the most cited
   ones in the middle of the block. #}
<div class="cm-wc-cloud {{ frameClass|default('') }}" data-word-cloud-live-target="cloud" data-scale="{{ scale.value }}">
    {% for word in words %}
        <span class="cm-wc-word cm-wc-word--{{ word.step }}" style="font-size: {{ word.size }}px;">{{ word.word }}</span>
    {% endfor %}
</div>
